<FluentStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" VerticalGap="16px" Class="my-2">
    <FluentMessageBar Intent="MessageBarIntent.Info">
        Training is one of the few areas of the app that's location-scoped. Don't assume the same
        rules apply elsewhere, most other modules (Clients, Zones, Automation, Dashboards) aren't
        split by location the way Training is.
    </FluentMessageBar>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">Ownership and sharing</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        Every course belongs to exactly one location. By default, only that location can see or
        manage it. Turning on <strong>Share this course across all locations</strong> makes it
        visible to every other location too, but strictly read-only there, other locations can
        view and preview it, but can't edit its content, change its auto-assign rule, or delete
        it. Only the owning location (or an Admin) can make changes.
    </FluentText>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">Managers vs Admins</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        A Manager only manages courses and assignments belonging to their own location, including
        bulk-assigning by role, which for a Manager only ever reaches people at their own
        location. Admins can act across every location, and are the only role that can move a
        course to a different owning location.
    </FluentText>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">Assignment location vs course location</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        An assignment records the location of whoever assigned it, which isn't always the same as
        the course's own owning location, this matters mainly for a shared course, where a
        Manager at a different location may have assigned it to one of their own staff.
    </FluentText>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">"Couldn't work out which location" error</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        Any Training page can occasionally fail to resolve which location you're working in and
        show this error instead of its usual content. It's normally temporary, use the
        <strong>Reload</strong> button that appears with it, or sign out and back in if it
        persists.
    </FluentText>
</FluentStack>
